<title>JAPAN: IDC sees printer market at 76.5 mln units in 2001.</title>
<headline>IDC sees printer market at 76.5 mln units in 2001.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Data Corp (IDC) said on Tuesday that it expects the worldwide market for printers to grow to 76.5 million units in 2001, up from 43.3 million units in 1996.</p>
<p>Angele Boyd, analyst at the industry research firm, said at a conference in Tokyo that major printer manufacturers, such as Fujitsu Ltd and Hewlett-Packard Co, are expected in late 1997 to introduce printers with the same printing speed but lower prices than existing machines.</p>
<p>Such developments will affect shipment volumes, she said.</p>
</text>
